// ============================================================================
// Gotek_JC3248_Test.ino  —  HARDWARE DIAGNOSTIC for the Guition JC3248W535(C)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Purpose: chase the "boots once then freezes after the loader" reports on
// newer JC3248W535C boards. Strips 5.9.4 down to just the hardware bring-up and
// reports what esptool-style board ID data we can read from the chip itself
// (model / silicon revision / PSRAM / flash / MAC), then runs selectable tests.
//
// Two suspects, both testable here: (1) PSRAM init failing on a new die rev
// (the real firmware's framebuffer is a 307KB ps_malloc with NO null-check, so
// a PSRAM failure = silent freeze on the first draw); (2) a timing / digitizer
// conflict — the AXS15231B is ONE chip doing both the QSPI display and the I2C
// touch (0x3B), so bus/clock timing can upset it.
//
// EVERYTHING here draws from INTERNAL RAM only (strip blits), so the panel still
// shows a result even if PSRAM is dead. Full detail goes to Serial.
//
// ARDUINO IDE BOARD SETTINGS (important):
//   Board: ESP32S3 Dev Module
//   USB CDC On Boot: ENABLED   <-- so the Serial Monitor works (firmware has it OFF)
//   USB Mode: USB-OTG (TinyUSB) ... or Hardware CDC, either is fine for serial
//   PSRAM: OPI PSRAM   |   Flash: 16MB (128Mb) QIO 80MHz   |   CPU: 240MHz
//   (this mirrors the real firmware so we reproduce the same PSRAM path)
//
// Put a text file  config.test  on the SD root to pick the mode + clocks.
// ============================================================================

